---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Sum of First n Terms of an AP | Class 10 Mathematics | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn sum formulas Sₙ = n/2[2a + (n-1)d] and Sₙ = n/2[a + L] for an Arithmetic Progression with step-by-step NCERT solved word problems."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/arithmetic-progressions" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Arithmetic Progressions</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">03</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 03 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Sum of First <span>n Terms</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master sum formulas Sₙ = n/2[2a + (n-1)d] and Sₙ = n/2[a + L] to calculate total values and solve NCERT word problems.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · THE FORMULAS -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · KEY FORMULAS</div>
					<h2>Formulas for Sum of n Terms (Sₙ)</h2>
					<p>
						The sum of the first <em>n</em> terms of an AP with first term <em>a</em> and common difference <em>d</em> is given by:
					</p>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>Sₙ = (n / 2) [ 2a + (n - 1)d ]</strong>
						<strong>Sₙ = (n / 2) [ a + L ]</strong>
						<span>Use the second formula when the last term <em>L</em> (or <em>aₙ</em>) is known!</span>
					</div>

					<div class="idea-box">
						<div class="idea-icon">💡</div>
						<div class="idea-content">
							<strong>Relationship Between aₙ and Sₙ</strong>
							<p>
								The <em>n-th term</em> of an AP can also be found from the sum of terms using:
								<br/>
								<strong>aₙ = Sₙ - Sₙ₋₁</strong>
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLES</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<!-- Example 1 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>Find the sum of the first 22 terms of the AP: 8, 3, -2...</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Given: a = 8, d = 3 - 8 = -5, n = 22.</p>
							<p>Using <em>Sₙ = (n/2) [2a + (n - 1)d]</em>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								S₂₂ = (22 / 2) [ 2(8) + (22 - 1)(-5) ]<br/>
								S₂₂ = 11 [ 16 + 21(-5) ]<br/>
								S₂₂ = 11 [ 16 - 105 ] = 11 × (-89) = <strong>-979</strong>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Example 2 -->
					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 2 (NCERT WORD PROBLEM)</span>
							<h3>Find the sum of first 1000 positive integers</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<p>Let S = 1 + 2 + 3 + ... + 1000. Here, a = 1, L = 1000, n = 1000.</p>
							<p>Using <em>Sₙ = (n/2) [a + L]</em>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								S₁₀₀₀ = (1000 / 2) [ 1 + 1000 ]<br/>
								S₁₀₀₀ = 500 × 1001 = <strong>500500</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">General Formula for sum of first <em>n</em> positive integers: <strong>Sₙ = n(n + 1) / 2</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Standard sum formula: <strong>Sₙ = (n/2)[2a + (n-1)d]</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Short formula when last term <em>L</em> is given: <strong>Sₙ = (n/2)[a + L]</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Finding a term from sum: <strong>aₙ = Sₙ - Sₙ₋₁</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/nth-term" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>nth Term of an AP</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/pyqs" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">ARITHMETIC PROGRESSIONS</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 03 of 04</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
							<div style="width: 75%;"></div>
						</div>

						<div class="sidebar-lessons">
							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/introduction" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>01</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Introduction to AP</strong>
									<small>First term (a) & difference (d)</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/nth-term" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>02</span>
								<div>
									<strong>nth Term of an AP</strong>
									<small>Formula aₙ = a + (n-1)d</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/sum-of-n-terms" class="sidebar-lesson active">
								<span>03</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Sum of First n Terms</strong>
									<small>Formula Sₙ = n/2[2a+(n-1)d]</small>
								</div>
							</a>

							<a href="/arithmetic-progressions/pyqs" class="sidebar-lesson">
								<span>04</span>
								<div>
									<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
									<small>CBSE 2020-2024 practice set</small>
								</div>
							</a>
						</div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</section>
		</div>
	</main>

	<style>
		.lesson-page {
